# Git's line-ending behaviour must not be able to decide whether a gate passes.
#
# Prettier sets endOfLine: lf. core.autocrlf is true on Windows. Without this
# file, git checks out CRLF for every text file, Prettier then rejects all of
# them, and the resulting failure is indistinguishable from a real formatting
# problem.
#
# Two symptoms, one cause, both machine-dependent:
#   - format:check is green on whoever last ran prettier --write and red on
#     every fresh Windows clone.
#   - schema-generation.spec.ts compares the checked-in schema.prisma against
#     what the generator writes. Content is byte-identical; the line endings are
#     not. Tracked as TODO.md ARC-09-9, which recorded it for the ERD work and
#     reached the same conclusion from the format:check side.
#
# The failure is invisible on a machine whose working tree happens to hold LF,
# which is why it survived. It is only ever observed on someone else's checkout.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never line-ending translated, never diffed as text.
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.webp     binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.ttf      binary
*.eot      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.zip      binary
*.gz       binary

# Excalidraw and Prisma sources are text and must stay LF. They are listed
# explicitly because a future contributor editing .gitattributes could
# reasonably decide a "diagram" or a "generated schema" is binary, and that
# decision would silently reintroduce the failure above.
*.excalidraw text eol=lf
*.prisma    text eol=lf
